---
description: Standing working agreements for every agent in this repository
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` first; it is the shared source of working instructions. These agreements
restate Curt's standing preferences for tools that load rules rather than `AGENTS.md`.

- **No branches unless Curt asks.** Work on the current branch, normally `main`.
- **Commit only when asked; never push unless asked.** A push to `main` deploys the site.
- **Curt switches among agents.** Codex, Claude, Devin and Cursor all work here, and the
  agent that commits is often not the one that wrote the change. Never treat commit author,
  committer or trailers as evidence of who wrote something; session transcripts decide
  (`scripts/production_history.py`).
- **Ask before acting on anything that needs approval.** Write a proposal in `proposals/`
  (see `proposals/README.md`) for frozen files, the story contract, invariants, CI,
  deletions or renumbering, reinterpreting a plan or owner decision, or unsettled editorial
  choices. Add opinions to other agents' proposals; only Curt decides.
- **Show sources' exact words.** Curt wants more transparency about sources than agents
  default to: quote exact wording as far as fair use allows when it helps a reader trace a
  detail to its origin. Register every quotation. Use a 256t pointer when you cannot write the
  words out. Never describe wording that could be shown. Paraphrase or redaction needs a named
  hazard (see `AGENTS.md`, "Lean toward transparency", 15 September 2026).
- **Leave other agents' work alone.** Other sessions may be editing at the same time: check
  `git --no-optional-locks status --short` before editing and preserve changes you did not
  make.
